{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BDa77fgtVaACbGjwUhveU5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations diverge on edge cases. This project stress-tests the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation system by deriving specs from C source, generating Go implementations, and verifying parity via differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** A four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify) produces Go binaries in `cmd/` backed by shared libraries in `pkg/` (sys, format, testutils). Specs live in `docs/`. The mage-claude-orchestrator drives synthesis from PRDs; differential testing in `pkg/testutils/` gates acceptance.\n\n**Current state:** Specifications are complete for multiple utilities (ts, cat, wc, sponge, du, ls). Generated code exists only at `generation-merged` tags — the working branch (`generation-gh-262-codegen`) has no generated code. Foundation packages (pkg/sys, pkg/format, pkg/testutils) and several cmd/ utilities have code at those tags but not on the branch.\n\n**Current release scope:** Release 01.3 — `du` specification and differential test. The single use case `rel01.3-uc001-du` has `spec_complete` status with code not started.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 01.3 is the target. It contains one use case: `rel01.3-uc001-du`. The du spec (PRD, use case, test suite) is complete. The next step is implementation. Per P2, implementation and tests must be separate tasks. With a 1-task limit, I propose the core `cmd/du` implementation. Since no `pkg/` code exists on the working branch, du must compile using only Go standard library packages.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/du implementation -- rel01.3-uc001-du core disk usage traversal and reporting\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ component structure, pkg/sys scope, design decisions)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.3-uc001-du.yaml (du use case and execution flow)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.3.yaml (du test suite, input/output expectations, PRD cross-references)\n      - \"docs/specs/product-requirements/ (locate the du PRD: glob for prd*-du.yaml)\"\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/du/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"du utility: flag parsing, recursive directory traversal, disk usage reporting\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement recursive directory traversal that computes disk usage per directory subtree using stat block counts (Stat_t.Blocks * 512 bytes), not FileInfo.Size() byte counts\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement output control flags: -a/--all (report all files, not just directories), -s/--summarize (report only total per argument), -c/--total (append grand total line), -d/--max-depth=N (limit reporting depth)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement size formatting flags: -h/--human-readable (K/M/G/T powers of 1024), -k (1024-byte blocks, default), -m (1048576-byte blocks), -b/--bytes (apparent size in bytes using FileInfo.Size())\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement error handling: on EACCES or EPERM during traversal, print diagnostic to stderr and continue; exit 0 if no errors, exit 1 if any errors occurred during traversal\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use filepath.WalkDir for directory traversal (Go 1.16+ efficient walker that avoids unnecessary stat calls on directory entries)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Access Stat_t fields via fi.Sys().(*syscall.Stat_t) for Blocks, Nlink, Dev, and Ino; use the syscall standard library package\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Track hard links by (Dev, Ino) pair in a map to count multiply-linked files only once\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Import only Go standard library packages (os, path/filepath, fmt, syscall, flag, strings, io). Do not import pkg/sys or pkg/format -- those packages may not exist on the working branch per ARCHITECTURE.yaml implementation_status\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/du/main.go compiles successfully with go build ./cmd/du/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"du <directory> prints one line per subdirectory with disk usage in 1024-byte blocks and the path, plus a total line for the argument\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"-s flag suppresses per-subdirectory output and prints only the total for each argument\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"-c flag appends a final line with the grand total across all arguments labeled 'total'\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"-h flag formats sizes with human-readable suffixes (K, M, G, T) using powers of 1024\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"Hard-linked files (Nlink > 1) contribute their block count only once per unique (Dev, Ino) pair\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"Permission-denied errors print a diagnostic to stderr and do not halt traversal; exit code is 1 when any error occurred\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15832,"cache_read_input_tokens":19286,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15832,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05d03e1e-981e-4f1c-912c-e17da87cab28","uuid":"1bb6eb77-4d71-4f02-ab9e-740761624e2f"}
